Ken Arromdee plugs his 'fruit' option:
> How about naming your fruit?  If you name your fruit "pomegranate"
> or whatever, and die and leave a ghost level, any fruits you leave
> behind _retain_the_name_.  Whoever finds the ghost level will find
> all your pomegranates....

When we NetHack gods were out creating the world, Ken added the
'fruit' name option. And it was fun.

But, noted i, the function to add a name to the fruit name table did
no range checking. Theoretically, you could enter 'Ofruit=' with 256
different (for duplicates were checked) fruit names, you could
overflow the table.

Code-weary Ken asserted that one who tried to overflow the table,
deserved to.  Besides, he doubted that anyone could conceive of so
many fruit names, leastwise without becoming bored long before.

I demonstrated otherwise. NetHack now overwrites old names at 257.

So without further ado, i give you:
